      "id": 1,
      "text": "North Miami Beach was originally called Fulford‑by‑the‑Sea when Captain William H. founded it in 1926.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Miami_Beach%2C_Florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city adopted the name North Miami Beach in 1931 after the state legislature granted a new charter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Miami_Beach%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original street grid, laid out in 1917, still shows wide avenues like Fulford Boulevard, now Northeast 172nd Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.citynmb.com/596/Our-History",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "North Miami Beach celebrated its 100th anniversary in 2025‑26 with a year‑long series of events and storytelling initiatives.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nmbcentennial.com/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The city’s public library opened in 1959 inside a storefront on NE 163rd Street and became independent in 1961.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
